# What ships to nfl.propbetedge.ai.
#
# The deployment is a static root: anything not listed here is publicly
# readable at its repository path. Internal engineering artefacts are excluded
# from the DEPLOYMENT, which is the only reliable control — a rewrite runs
# after the static filesystem and cannot shadow a file that is really there.
#
# tests/nfl-public-surface.test.mjs classifies every tracked file against these
# rules and fails if an internal path would ship or a required asset would not.
# scripts/public-surface-gate.mjs proves the same against production.

# Stadium masters stay in the repo as sources but are not deployed. The product
# ships stadiums/*-bg.webp, *-bgsm.webp and *-thumb.webp, generated from these.
stadiums/*.jpg

# Football history graph: design, schema and policy code. Source only, never served.
history/

# --- internal engineering artefacts -----------------------------------------
docs/
migrations/
research/
scripts/
tests/
.github/
release/
.css-ownership.json

# Planning, design and audit notes, wherever they live.
*.md

# --- Cloudflare Worker source ------------------------------------------------
# Worker code, wrangler.toml (which carries the Cloudflare account id) and
# worker tests are operated from the repository, never from the web
# deployment. The one exception is the shared engine library: api/home-market.js
# and api/pbe-picks.js import it at build time, so that directory still ships
# (minus its tests). Every other worker directory is named explicitly, and a
# test fails if a new worker is added without a rule here.
workers/nfl-auth/
workers/nfl-billing/
workers/nfl-current/
workers/nfl-game-grader/
workers/nfl-game-picks-orchestrator/
workers/nfl-gateway/
workers/nfl-intel/
workers/nfl-odds/
workers/nfl-odds-snapshot/
workers/nfl-picks/
workers/nfl-prop-picks-grader/
workers/nfl-prop-picks-orchestrator/
workers/nfl-prop-picks-shared/
workers/nfl-prop-picks-tuner/
workers/nfl-replay/
workers/nfl-schedule/
workers/nfl-td-targets-shared/
workers/nfl-touchdown-targets-grader/
workers/nfl-touchdown-targets-orchestrator/
workers/nfl-touchdown-targets-tuner/
workers/nfl-weight-tuner/
workers/nfl-picks-engine-shared/tests/

# --- derived datasets the runtime never reads --------------------------------
# api/* reads exactly eight files from data/dist with readFileSync, so those stay.
data/dist/active-*.json
data/dist/media-coverage*.json
data/dist/*-coverage-audit.json
data/dist/qbdna-demo/
